-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",40,{
[1249]="70055078\n1\tExamine the markings near the slain Rangers\tYou should examine the markings near the slain Rangers in the Circle of Death.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the fell beast that slew many Rangers of Ithilien.\n",
[1250]="70022D38\n1\tTalk to Gronu at his camp\tGronu's camp is just south of the river, in a small grove of trees, north of Harndirion. Culang has asked you to seek out the wounded hunter Gronu, who may need assistance.\n",
[1251]="700344EB\n1\tSearch nearby for signs of the horse's rider\tSigns of the rider may be found near the horse's corpse in the southern Whitshaws. You should search near the wintry landmark for any signs of whoever braved such a dangerous errand.\n2\tSearch nearby for signs of the horse's rider\tSigns of the rider may be found near the horse's corpse in the southern Whitshaws. You should search near the wintry landmark for any signs of whoever braved such a dangerous errand.\n3\tSearch nearby for signs of the horse's rider\tSigns of the rider may be found near the horse's corpse in the southern Whitshaws. You should search near the wintry landmark for any signs of whoever braved such a dangerous errand.\n4\tSearch the rider\tSigns of the rider may be found west of the horse's corpse in the southern Whitshaws. You should search near the smashed boulders for signs of what became of the pursued and fleeing rider.\n5\tPick up the messenger's missive\tThe message borne by the rider has fallen not far from his side. You should pick up the message and see if you can bear it yourself, and fulfil the errand for which this poor man died.\n6\tRead the missive\tThe missive is in your inventory. You should read the missive found on the dead rider.\n7\tCompleted\tCyneberg has ridden on to the village of Dunfast in the central Whitshaws. You should bring the missive to Dunfast and show it to Cyneberg, and hopefully evacuate the people there if it is not too late.\n",
[1252]="70034556\n1\tDestroy Orc-tents and bonfires\tOrc-tents and bonfires can be found at the ice-spire left in Núrzum's wake. You should tear down the tents and bonfires of the Orcs.\n2\tDestroy Orc bonfires (total: 3)\030Destroy Orc tents (total: 6)\tOrc-tents and bonfires can be found at the ice-spire left in Núrzum's wake. You should tear down the tents and bonfires of the Orcs.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have torn down the comforts of the unguarded Orcs settling in Núrzum's shadow. No Orcs will settle openly in Wildermore while its people still inhabit these lands.\n",
[1253]="7000F237\n1\tFind Reginald Ward's missing herald\tReginald's herald was lost somewhere on the ice-shelf, south-east of Sûri-kylä, on the eastern edge of the Ice Bay of Forochel. Reginald Ward is at Sûri-kylä, north-west of the ice-shelf. Reginald Ward asked you search for his herald and return him to Sûri-kylä.\n",
[1254]="70040A55\n1\tAnswer the summons from the Corsair at the gate\tThe Corsair seeking you is at the main gate of Calembel in Lamedon. You should answer the summons of the Corsair, and find out what he wants.\n2\tSee what Jajax wants\tJajax is at the gate of Calembel. You should speak with Jajax.\n3\tMeet Jajax at the site of Hebil's massacre\tThe site of Hebil's massacre is south-west of Calembel. You should go with Jajax to the site where Hebil slaughtered Jajax's men. NOTE: Use the whistle to summon Jajax if you become separated.\n4\tHelp Jajax avenge his men\tThe site of Hebil's massacre is south-west of Calembel. You should help Jajax avenge his men against Hebil. NOTE: Use the whistle to summon Jajax if you become separated.\n5\tCompleted\tThe Havens of Belfalas can be found by following the road south-west from Lamedon. You should travel to the Havens of Belfalas.\n",
[1255]="7002C388\n1\tDefeat wolves (total: 12)\tBrifard has advised you to hunt down wolves in the nearby wolf-den to the north-east. This particular wolf-den has been nicknamed 'The Murderous Pit' by the Rohirrim of Stangard. Brifard wants you to cull the wolf-pack in response to their violence.\n2\tTalk to Brifard\tBrifard is located at the camp-site to the south-east of Thinglad. You should return to Brifard with news of your success.\n",
[1256]="7002EE2E\n1\tQuestion the farmer about the attack\tThe farmer whose lands were looted can be found west of Langhold, not far from the north gate. You should speak with the farmer and hear out the story of what befell him.\n2\tFind the brigand camp\tEastmund's Lair is along the western edge of the northern Wold.\n3\tConfront the leader of the brigands about the group's aggressive positioning\tThe foes amassed near Langhold appear to be very organized. You should seek the leader of this rabble and encourage him to return with his unruly followers to exile.\n4\tBring Eastmund's message to the Thane\tEastmund has asked for a message of grievances to be brought to Thane Utred of Langhold. You should go to Thane Utred at once and deliver the message, and warn him of the forbidding brigand presence near Langhold.\n5\tShow the letter to Cíllan\tCíllan stands near the Thane in the Mead Hall of Langhold. You should show Cíllan the letter.\n6\tSee if Utred heeds the warning after receiving his wife's counsel\tUtred is in the Mead Hall in Langhold. You should speak with Thane Utred now that Cíllan has said her piece.\n",
[1257]="700303BF\n1\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. Gísling worries that his father's actions have hurt his station within the Sutcrofts and asks that you aid Fastred further as a gesture of good will.\n2\tSearch central Snowbourn for evidence of a spy\tThe oven can be found in central Snowbourn to the east of the Mead Hall. Fastred has sent you in search of information about a potential threat to Snowbourn. Fastred mentioned that your search should begin near the oven as the spy has been tampering with food.\n3\tExamine the crumpled note near the oven\tThe note can be found on a stool next to the oven in central Snowbourn. You have not found anyone acting suspiciously, but a hastily-scrawled note near the oven catches your eye.\n4\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. You have found an anonymous note that asserts Gísling is a traitor to the Sutcrofts and warns Fastred himself to not trust his Thane's son.\n5\tTalk to Gísling in Snowbourn\tGísling can be found in the northern part of Snowbourn. Fastred wishes to hear Gísling's thoughts on the note you discovered.\n6\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. Gísling bade you return to Fastred with his response.\n",
[1258]="7002F97F\n1\tDefeat the White Hand pillagers at each farmstead\tThe abandoned farmsteads can be found south of Cliving, west of the road. Each farmstead has been occupied by a single White Hand pillager, who has recruited others to help defile the lands.\n2\tThe abandoned farmsteads can be found south of Cliving, west of the road. Each farmstead has been occupied by a single White Hand pillager, who has recruited others to help defile the lands.\t\n3\tTalk to Captain Garmund outside of Cliving\tCaptain Garmund can be found at the western watch-tower, just west of Cliving. Garmund will be most appreciative of your efforts to remove the White Hand Orcs from the occupied farmhouses.\n",
[1259]="70009983\n1\tThe encampment of the giants is at Amon Môth, south and west of the Eavespires. Lithuifin has asked you to pour his draught into the giants' stew.\t\n2\tTalk to Lithuifin at the Eavespires\tLithuifin is at the Eavespires, north and east of Amon Môth. You should return to Lithuifin with your report.\n",
[1260]="7004A8D3\n1\tExamine slain Orcs on the road to Durthang (total: 4)\tSlain Orcs can be found on the road to Durthang, slightly to the north and west of the ruined encampment. Legolas has asked you to examine the slain Orcs along the road to Lhingris to discover if Ungwetári has set her children upon the Orcs of Mordor.\n2\tExamine the uneaten Orc on the road to Durthang\tThe uneaten Orc can be found beneath an archway on the road to Durthang, slightly to the north and west of the ruined encampment. You have examined the slain Orcs near Legolas's encampment, but you have noticed one who does not appear to have been devoured.\n3\tTalk to Legolas at the ruined encampment\tLegolas can be found at the ruined encampment along the road to Durthang in Lhingris. While spiders have slain many of the Orcs in Lhingris, it appears that some Orcs have begun to fight amongst themselves as well. You should return to Legolas.\n",
[1261]="7006AE8D\n1\tSearch for Baziphâr below Dâr Laja in Tâkhdar\tBaziphâr is likely still hiding in Tâkhdar, below Dâr Laja. Find Baziphâr and scold him for hiding below the city.\n2\tScold Baziphâr and convince him to return home\tBaziphâr is likely still hiding in Tâkhdar below Dâr Laja. Find Baziphâr and scold him for hiding below the city.\n3\tSpeak with Baziphâr\tBaziphâr is still hiding in Tâkhdar below Dâr Laja.\n4\tSpeak with Hanâth\tHanâth is waiting at The Din of Arms in the Tor-gardens, in the western side of Umbar Baharbêl. Hanâth will surely be grateful to hear her husband has returned home.\n",
[1262]="70015E38\n1\tThe summoning horn is inside the southern entrance to the ruins of Pembar, north-east of Echad Eregion. Faenhilith has asked you to return to Pembar and use the Orkish summoning horn to challenge the leader of the half-orcs.\t\n2\tTalk to Faenhilith at Echad Eregion\tFaenhilith is at Echad Eregion, south-west of Pembar. You should return to Faenhilith with news of your victory against Fauldush.\n",
[1263]="7002EF77\n1\tFind the source of the watchman's dread in the Easterling encampment\tThe Easterling camp can be found at the South Undeep.\n2\tPeek into the hole in the fence\tA fenced-in area can be found behind the Easterling camp at the South Undeep. You should peek into the fenced-in area to see if anything is amiss.\n3\tReturn at once to Adbert to warn him\tAdbert is at his post at the Undeep Watch. You should return to Adbert with news of the Nazgûl's presence in the Easterling camp, along with the brigands poised to attack Langhold with aid from Mordor.\n",
[1264]="70058FDF\n1\tIgnite barrels of black-fire in Orkish trenches (total: 8)\tBarrels of black-fire can be found in Orkish trenches in the War of Three Peaks. You have discovered barrels of black-fire used by the Orcs of Gundabad. You should ignite their barrels and sow chaos among the ranks of their forces before these explosives can be used against the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ.\n2\tTalk to Reithvald Red-ember\tReithvald Red-ember can be found at Ifbar-athrâkh. You have ignited and destroyed many barrels of black-fire in the Orkish trenches around Zudramdân. You should report news of your success to Reithvald Red-ember.\n",
[1265]="70061443\n1\tCollect the 'filled' satchel from Postman Twofoot's table\tThe route to Nobottle begins at Waymeet, continues into Needlehole, and passes through the Rushock Gate into Yondershire. You have prepared a satchel containing Postmaster Proudfoot's letter to be taken on the Quick Post's route to Nobottle. You should pick up the 'filled' satchel from Postman Twofoot's table and carry it along the route to Nobottle by way of the Rushock Gate. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Bounder Dogberry at the Rushock Gate\tBounder Dogberry can be found at the Rushock Gate, just to the north-west of Needlehole in the Shire. While attempting to complete the route to Nobottle, you have been stopped by Bounder Dogberry at the Rushock Gate. You should talk to Bounder Dogberry.\n3\tWait for Bounder Dogberry to finish his inspection\tBounder Dogberry can be found at the Rushock Gate, just to the north-west of Needlehole in the Shire. Bounder Dogberry has demanded to inspect the contents of the satchel you are carrying to Nobottle. You should wait for Bounder Dogberry to finish his inspection.\n4\tTalk to Bounder Dogberry at the Rushock Gate\tBounder Dogberry can be found at the Rushock Gate, just to the north-west of Needlehole in the Shire. Bounder Dogberry has laid claim to Postmaster Proudfoot's letter and the satchel. You should talk to Bounder Dogberry.\n5\tTalk to Postmaster Proudfoot in Michel Delving\tPostmaster Proudfoot can be found outside the Quick Post in Michel Delving. The Postmaster's letter was confiscated by Bounder Dogberry on behalf of the Chief Shirriff. You should return to Postmaster Proudfoot and tell him what has happened.\n6\tTalk to Mayor Will Whitfoot in Michel Delving\tMayor Will Whitfoot can be found outside the Town Hole, in Michel Delving. After learning that someone claiming to be the \"Chief Shirriff\" has been interfering with the Quick Post, Postmaster Proudfoot has insisted that you speak to Mayor Will Whitfoot. You should talk to Mayor Will Whitfoot.\n",
[1266]="70030B6C\n1\tTalk to the stranger\tA strange man sits atop an avanc in the distance - you should speak to him, for surely he is an interesting fellow.\n2\tTalk to the stranger\tThe stranger is located in western Sutcrofts along the shore by the Entwade.\n",
[1267]="70034C20\n1\tDefeat White Hand Orcs near Thrymm's Camp (total: 4)\tOrcs roam the Writhendowns in great numbers, prowling to and fro -- as Thrymm described. You should defeat Orcs as you roam the Writhendowns.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of scouting Orcs at the Wold-Writhendowns border, but the enemy presence still presses upon the land.\n",
[1268]="70033232\n1\tFind the first source of the odour\tThe odour seems to be wafting from the southern area of the great tree-lined courtyard in Nud-melek. Svanr wants you to investigate the odour that occasionally sneaks up to disturb his silent homage.\n2\tFind the second source of the odour\tThe odour wafts from the courtyard's southern edge in Nud-melek. You should examine the second source of the odour.\n3\tFind the third source of the odour\tThe odour wafts from the courtyard's southern edge in Nud-melek. You should examine the third source of the odour.\n4\tCompleted\tYou have discovered three clusters of Fungus in the Second Hall of Nud-melek.\n",
[1269]="7003578B\n1\tSearch the Orc-roadway for signs of the White Hand\tThe Orc-roadway can be found to the west of Barallas and the other Ents. Barallas has asked that you return to the Orc-roadway and see if the White Hand still holds firm control of the path.\n2\tFollow the Orc-roadway to the north-west\tThe Orc-roadway continues to the north and west. Having discovered a few Orc-stragglers, but no larger force, you should continue following the road deeper into the Balewood.\n3\tFollow the Orc-roadway further into north-west Balewood\tThe Orc-roadway continues to the west. You have discovered the grim remains of a fight between the denizens of the Balewood and the White Hand. You should continue up the path to the west.\n4\tFollow the Orc-roadway further up the hill\tThe Orc-roadway through the Balewood continues up the hill to the west. The roadway is strangely clear here, but you should investigate the gruff voices you hear further up the hill.\n5\tTalk to Barallas outside Drû Vádokan\tBarallas can be found to the south of Drû Vádokan. Barallas and the other Ents will be curious to learn what you have discovered along the roadway. Barallas has travelled to meet you near the White Hand camp.\n",
[1270]="70032BDB\n1\tDefeat the White Hand tactician\030Defeat the Moria task-master\tThe Orc leaders are located somewhere within their tribe's encampment.\n2\tFind Knakk's camp-site\tKnakk is located on the elevated platform just north of the White Hand Orcs' encampment, on the road toward the Grand Stair. He has remained hidden from the Orcs so far, but their scouts have almost found him a few times. He will be happy to know they are going to be far less organized for some time, thanks to you.\n",
[1271]="70022B2D\n1\tDefeat ancient Barrow-wights (total: 20)\tAncient Barrow-wights can be found within the Maze Wing of the Great Barrow.\n",
[1272]="7005AB07\n1\tCollect ancient dwarf weapons (total: 8)\030Collect ancient dwarf armour (total: 6)\tYou have discovered ancient dwarf-made equipment inside Draurákh. You should collect ancient dwarf armour and ancient dwarf weapons and return them to Fellgát.\n2\tTalk to Dréri at Fellgát\tYou have collected several pieces of ancient dwarf-made equipment. You should return to Fellgát and show it to Dréri.\n",
[1273]="70022B2A\n1\tSet flame to the wrapped ancient corpses (total: 10)\tThe ancient corpses can be found throughout the Maze wing of the Great Barrow.\n",
[1274]="70022B47\n1\tLight the ancient braziers (total: 4)\tAncient braziers can be found within the Flooded Wing of the Great Barrow. You need to light the ancient braziers of the Great Barrow.\n",
[1275]="70008B82\n1\tTalk to Atli Spider-bane\tAtli Spider-bane is in the town of Archet, in Bree-land, far to the west of the Misty Mountains. Sigrun and Greip learned that an evil plague of spiders has taken root in caverns beneath Helegrod, and their fell queen is known to Atli Spider-bane.\n",
[1276]="700001BA\n1\tFind Bethad in the Gorthorog-cave\tThe Gorthorog-cave is in Malenhad, east of Aughaire. Fonn has asked you to explore a cave in Malenhad to which Gertheryg have been seen travelling.\n2\tTalk to Bethad\tBethad is in the Gorthorog-cave in Malenhad, east of Aughaire. At Fonn's request, you searched the Gorthorog-cave for Bethad. You have found him, but he appears wounded.\n",
[1277]="7000D7A2\n1\tFind Bethad in Ologfil\tFonn has asked you to explore the caves of Ologfil in Malenhad to the north of Tyrn Lhuig, to determine the fate of Bethad who was investigating the presence of gertheryg.\n2\tSpeak with Fonn in Tyrn Lhuig\tSpeak with Fonn in Tyrn Lhuig and tell him of Bethad's rescue.\n",
[1278]="70025A51\n1\tThe lighthouse is at the northern edge of the Barandalf, south-east of the colossus. Gaelnarthan asked you to venture to the ruins of an ancient lighthouse and find any remains of the log-books kept there.\t\n2\tBring what you found to Gaelnarthan\tGaelnarthan is at the Colossus, north-west of the lighthouse ruins. Gaelnarthan will be eager to examine the page you found.\n",
[1279]="7001AACA\n1\tExamine Silvan records (total: 8)\tThe Wild Ruins lie to the south of Ost Galadh. Agorin has asked you to examine and record the records of the Silvan Elves of Ost Galadh in the Wild Ruins.\n2\tTalk to Agorin at Ost Galadh\tAgorin is at Ost Galadh, north of the Wild Ruins. You should return to Agorin at and tell her what you discovered about the records of the Silvan Elves that once inhabited this place.\n",
[1280]="7000EC09\n1\tThrow feathers at Reodh Fuil\030Place the fish by the bay\tThe ritual stone is south along the Ice Bay among the Angmarim. Reodh Fuil is south east of Sûri-kylä. Jalmari instructed you to throw the feathers into the wind at Reodh Fuil and place the fish by the Ice Bay at the ritual stone that has now been overrun by Angmarim.\n2\tTalk to Jalmari\030Collect Ritual Bag\tJalmari is at Sûri-kylä on the north eastern edge of the Ice Bay of Forochel. You should return to Jalmari and tell him that you have done as he asked.\n",
})
